pages.content:
# PR #20 portable reproduction evidence

Analysis ID: 6bd5b334-b400-4b60-aa82-d573c85b982b. Exact source commit `2f47dd39058ea9c32fc13eefa413090dd8f0fcf0`; base and merge base `ad4308fa1f5bb3bfff043993ea162190d9375345`. Fixture SHA is the same reviewed PR head; fixture rows/bundles are synthetic.

135 existing unit tests passed (storage 18, mcp-schema 25, domain 45, MCP 47). Three focused database/MCP suites: 19 passed, 2 failed (catalog size and stale inventory). Five independent boundary probes: 3 desired-behavior failures, 2 controls passed. Two additional PostgreSQL probes both failed desired guarantees (archived public closure and completed evidence reassignment). Domain/storage/schema typechecks passed.

## Reproduction setup

Check out the exact SHA into a disposable checkout. Use Node 22.22.1, pnpm 11.9.0 and `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. The review reused installed lockfile dependencies; it did not reinstall all dependencies. Run package test:unit scripts, not root-relative CLI tests (their CWD matters). The standalone installer is exercised by the local-runtime package test.

For the independent probes below, save `review-probes.test.ts` at the disposable repository root. Create a Vitest config with exact source aliases for each @skillplane package (and specific exported subpaths before parent aliases); set test.include to that file. This prevents workspace links from loading another checkout. Run `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config review.config.ts`. Expected exit: 1; defects are asserted against desired behavior.

## Probe source

```typescript
import { it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { requiredScopesForRequest, principalForWorkspace } from './mcp/src/auth.ts';
import { requiredAction } from './packages/api/src/middleware/authorization.ts';
import { VerificationService } from './packages/domain/src/verification.ts';
import { CompositionService } from './packages/domain/src/composition-service.ts';
import { canonicalizeBundleFiles } from './packages/storage/src/index.ts';
const principal:any={kind:'user',actorId:'qa-user',userId:'qa-user',sessionId:'qa-session',workspaceId:'qa-workspace',role:'owner'};
it('new composition write tool requires OAuth write scope',async()=>{const request=new Request('https://example.test/mcp',{method:'POST',headers:{'content-type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:'2.0',id:1,method:'tools/call',params:{name:'skill_composition_candidate_create',arguments:{}}})});expect(await requiredScopesForRequest(request)).toContain('skills:write');});
it('user principal does not independently enforce token scopes (control)',async()=>{const services:any={controlDatabase:{pool:{query:async()=>({rows:[{role:'owner'}]})}}};const p=await principalForWorkspace(services,{kind:'user',userId:'qa-user',credentialId:'REDACTED',scopes:[]} as any,'qa-workspace','skills:write');expect(p?.kind).toBe('user');});
it('HTTP run list has a middleware read guard (reject bot false positive)',()=>{expect(requiredAction('/api/v1/skills/qa/verification-runs','GET')).toBe('skills:read');});
it('evidence fragment tokens are rejected before idempotency',async()=>{const v=new VerificationService({} as any,{} as any,{claim:async()=>({state:'replay',responseBody:{result:{id:'qa-run'}}})} as any);await expect(v.addEvidence({principal,idempotencyKey:'qa',requestId:'qa',runId:'qa-run',result:{claimId:'qa-claim',status:'pass',explanation:'REDACTED evidence',evidence:[{type:'runtime',uri:'https://example.test/run#token=REDACTED-secret',sha256:'a'.repeat(64),description:'REDACTED',redacted:true}]}})).rejects.toMatchObject({code:'VERIFICATION_INVALID'});});
it('global withdrawal blocks a still-public regional source',async()=>{const bundle=await canonicalizeBundleFiles({skill:{formatVersion:1,name:'QA',slug:'qa',description:'QA skill',tags:[],entrypoints:{execute:'SKILL.md'}},files:new Map([['SKILL.md',new TextEncoder().encode('Read carefully.')]])});const pool:any={query:async()=>({rows:[{id:'qa-version',workspace_id:'other-workspace',skill_id:'qa-skill',skill_slug:'qa',semantic_version:'1.0.0',content_digest:bundle.digest,r2_object_key:'REDACTED',visibility:'public',archived_at:null,status:'published',deprecated_at:null,revoked_at:null}]})};const control:any={query:async(sql:string)=>({rows:sql.includes('public_skill_version_lifecycle')?[{deprecated_at:null,revoked_at:null,withdrawn_sequence:'10'}]:[{slug:'qa-workspace'}]})};const svc=new CompositionService(pool,{getCanonicalBundle:async()=>({bytes:bundle.bytes})} as any,control);await expect((svc as any).source('qa-version',principal)).rejects.toMatchObject({code:'SKILL_DEPENDENCY_CONFLICT'});});

